---
import DocumentSection from "../components/DocumentSection.astro";
import DocumentLayout from "../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro";
---

<DocumentLayout
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy — Baros"
  description="Privacy Policy for Baros."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  intro="This policy explains how Baros handles workout data, account data, sync, export, and deletion."
>
  <DocumentSection title="Summary">
    <p>
      You can use Baros locally without creating an account. Signing in enables
      sync through Clerk authentication and Convex account-backed storage. You
      can export workout history and delete account-backed or local data from
      Settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Baros does not use third-party advertising, cross-app tracking, or product
      analytics in the v1 release.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Data stored locally">
    <p>
      Baros stores workout-related data such as exercises, sets, workout
      sessions, notes, settings, and workout history. You can use the app locally
      on your iPhone without creating an account.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Account and authentication">
    <p>
      If you create an account, Baros uses Clerk for authentication. Clerk may
      process account information such as your email address, authentication
      identifiers, session information, and Sign in with Apple details.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use Sign in with Apple and choose Hide My Email, Apple may provide
      a private relay email address instead of your personal email address.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Sync">
    <p>
      When you sign in, Baros uses Convex to sync supported workout, exercise,
      settings, and history data for your account. Sync data is scoped to your
      authenticated account.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Exporting and deleting your data">
    <ul>
      <li>You can export workout history from Settings.</li>
      <li>
        Signed-in users can delete their account and account-backed data from
        Settings under Privacy &amp; Data.
      </li>
      <li>
        Signed-out users can delete local data stored on the device from Settings
        under Privacy &amp; Data.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="No analytics, ads, or tracking">
    <p>
      Baros does not use third-party advertising, cross-app tracking, or product
      analytics in the v1 release. Standard platform and provider diagnostics may
      be processed by Apple, Clerk, Convex, or hosting providers to keep their
      services reliable and secure.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>

  <DocumentSection title="Contact">
    <p>
      For privacy questions or support, email <a
        href="mailto:support@tatooles.dev">support@tatooles.dev</a
      >.
    </p>
  </DocumentSection>
</DocumentLayout>
